  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 1222 PM MDT Tue Sep 8 2026\n\nStarting Friday, elongated zonal flow over Northern CONUS with \na possibility of two low pressure systems moving over the U.S. \nand Canadian border over the weekend and early next week. This \nwill allow possible chances for afternoon showers from embedded \nshortwave troughs and cooler temperatures as cold fronts could \npass by. On Friday night and into Saturday morning, there is \nhigh confidence (75%) that showers will be north of I-70. \nHowever, there is low to medium confidence (25-40%) that this \nwill be severe as the environment conditions will be unfavorable\nas wind shear will be disorganized and weak. The main potential\nhazard will be small hail as there is sufficient CAPE over 1000\nJ/kg and a high lapse rate. \n\nOver the weekend, there is low confidence (25%) for chances of\nsevere weather due to the lack of forcing. Saturday night,\nchances for storms will be relatively low, but will increase at\nmidnight near US 283. The main potential conditions of\ninterest are heavy rain and small hail. Precipitable water\n(PWats) is forecast to be in 1.55 inches, CAPE above 1200 J/kg,\nand a \"low\" melting layer below 16,000 feet. On Sunday, storms\nare possible again in the evening hours with chances ranging\nfrom 20 to 60%. For now, the better chances favor the northern\nhalf of the area. \n\nOn Monday and Tuesday, the chances for storms continue as a\npotential upper trough slices through the Northern U.S. While\nthere is variability on when the trough moves through the area,\nstorms are possible each day in the evening. Which ever day the\ntrough moves through will likely have a chance for severe\nweather. \n\nTemperatures will be fairly consistent Friday with highs in the\nmid 90s and then drop into the low 80s Saturday as the overnight\ncold front comes through. There is medium to high confidence\n(50-70%) that afternoon temperatures will stay in the 80s for\nthe remainder of the period as there is a large spread of 10F\ndegrees within the guidance that could put temperatures in the\nupper 80s. Otherwise temperatures will finally start to fall\nfrom the summer heat.",
